WEBVTT

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:13.859
Hi you guys, my name is Sarah and I'm from Montreal, Canada and I have been watching How I Met Your Mother since I was 13.
大家好，我叫莎拉，来自加拿大蒙特利尔，从 13 岁起我就一直在看《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:21.859
I've dealt with depression and loneliness on and off for the last 10 years or so and How I Met Your Mother is a Month.
在过去的十年左右的时间里，我断断续续地应对着抑郁和孤独，而《老爸老妈的浪漫史》就是一个月。

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:25.859
One of the very few TV shows that's helped me the most.
为数不多的对我帮助最大的电视节目之一。

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:41.859
They say that watching the same TV show is a form of self-soothing, partly because you know how the episode goes and how it will end, but also I would say because it feels like the characters are your friends and you're just hanging out with them.
他们说观看同一部电视节目是一种自我安慰，部分原因是你知道这一集的进展和结局，但我想说的是，因为感觉角色是你的朋友，你只是和他们一起出去玩。

00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:45.859
In some weird way, at least I like to think that.
以某种奇怪的方式，至少我喜欢这样认为。

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:51.899
And how I met your mother is like that for me, and well I'm grateful for it.
我是如何认识你母亲的，对我来说就是这样，对此我很感激。

00:00:51.899 --> 00:01:02.295
Many times I've had very dark moments in my life, but the jokes and heartaches of Paul and Mitch and other have been there to catch me.
很多时候，我的人生经历过非常黑暗的时刻，但保罗、米奇和其他人的笑话和心痛一直困扰着我。

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.760
So thank you for co-creating the show, Craig.
所以谢谢你共同创作了这个节目，克雷格。

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:15.462
Thank you, Josh, for playing my friend, Ted, and thank you to you both for creating and hosting this lovely deep dive podcast.
乔什，谢谢你扮演我的朋友泰德，也感谢你们创建和主持这个可爱的深度播客。

00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:26.011
I've been absolutely loving, listening to this whenever I can, as it's kind of like a second part to one of the shows that saved my life.
我非常喜欢，只要有机会就听这个，因为它有点像拯救我生命的节目之一的第二部分。

00:01:26.011 --> 00:01:29.400
So thank you truly and have a beautiful day.
衷心感谢您，祝您有美好的一天。

00:01:49.879 --> 00:01:52.134
Welcome to How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们如何成就了你的母亲》。

00:01:52.134 --> 00:01:53.165
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

