00:43:00.769 --> 00:43:02.289
But it was really sweet.
但真的很甜蜜。

00:43:02.289 --> 00:43:21.650
And there's something about, again, we talk a lot about people in, going through tough life transitions, but also like being overseas like in the armed forces and whether you're in like a really dangerous zone or a zone where kind of nothing's happening and you're away from your family.
再说一次，我们谈论了很多关于人们经历艰难的生活转变的事情，但也像在海外，比如在武装部队中，以及你是否处于一个真正危险的区域，或者一个什么都没有发生并且远离你的家人的区域。

00:43:21.650 --> 00:43:32.010
Like there's a lot that one might need some sense of comfort or familiarity or some sense of back-homeness.
就像人们可能需要一些舒适感、熟悉感或某种回家的感觉一样。

00:43:32.010 --> 00:43:37.489
We've heard this so many times about people and deployments around the world that this was the connection to home.
我们已经多次听到有关世界各地人员和部署的说法，这就是与家庭的联系。

00:43:37.489 --> 00:43:44.969
How much of it was a connection to home and that people would watch it together in barracks and like, and I don't know, that really warms my heart.
其中有多少是与家的联系，人们会在军营里一起观看它，我不知道，这真的温暖了我的心。

00:43:44.969 --> 00:43:45.809
I really love that.
我真的很喜欢那个。

00:43:45.809 --> 00:43:48.769
So thank you to everybody who has served our country.
因此，感谢所有为我们国家服务的人。

00:43:48.769 --> 00:43:49.650
Yeah, thanks Josh.
是的，谢谢乔希。

00:43:49.650 --> 00:43:57.610
Thanks for that letter and shout out to all the people overseas who are on military bases who are watching the show.
感谢您的这封信，并向所有在海外军事基地观看该节目的人们大声喊叫。

00:43:57.610 --> 00:44:01.489
And if you're loving this podcast, please spread the word.
如果您喜欢这个播客，请传播出去。

00:44:01.489 --> 00:44:06.130
We're so happy to spend this time with you and we'll see you next time.
我们很高兴与您共度这段时间，我们下次再见。

